The [[Eisenhower matrix|https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_management#The_Eisenhower_Method]]
(also known as the ''urgent-important matrix'') is a [[dashboard|$:/plugins/nico/projectify/doc/Dashboard]]
tab that helps you decide what to work on first. It displays your tasks in
four quadrants, based on how urgent and how important they are:

* ''Do first'' - important & urgent
* ''Schedule'' - important, but not urgent
* ''Delegate'' - urgent, but not important
* ''Eliminate'' - neither important nor urgent

To classify a task, simply [[drag & drop|https://tiddlywiki.com/#Drag%20and%20Drop]]
it from the [[Inbox|$:/plugins/nico/projectify/doc/Inbox]] into the quadrant of
your choice: the task leaves the Inbox and is stored in that quadrant. Tasks
can be dragged from one quadrant to another at any time, and the button
displayed next to a classified task moves it back to the Inbox.

<<py-tip "The quadrant of a task is stored in its `quadrant` field, which can be used in filters (for example `[tag[todo]quadrant[do]]`).">>
